import json
from pathlib import Path
C=[]
def clip(id,kind,title,voice,script,gist,options,ans,details,detail_options,detail_answers,phrases,reply,model,logo=None):
 C.append(dict(id=id,kind=kind,title=title,voice=voice,script=script,gist={'question':gist,'choices':options,'answer':ans},details=[{'question':q,'choices':o,'answer':a} for q,o,a in zip(details,detail_options,detail_answers)],phrases=phrases,response=reply,model=model,logo=logo))
clip('voice-date','client','The date is hard to read','Zoe (Premium)',"Hi, I've looked at the poster on my phone. The café name is clear, but I can barely read the opening date. Could you make that easier to see? I'd like to keep the warm colors and the gold line. Thanks. Send me a quick preview before you export the final file.",'What is the client mainly asking for?',['A more readable opening date.','A new café name.','A completely different palette.'],0,['Where did the client view the poster?','What should remain?'],[['On a phone.','On a street sign.','On printed packaging.'],['The warm colors and gold line.','Every unreadable text color.','Only the café name.']],[0,0],[['I can barely read','I can read it only with difficulty.'],['before you export','The client wants a preview before the final files.']],'Respond to the readability problem, preserve what the client likes, and confirm the proof.','I’ll make the opening date easier to read while keeping the warm palette and gold line. I’ll send a phone-size preview before exporting the final file.')
clip('voice-pop','client','“Make it pop” with a clue','Jamie (Premium)',"Thanks for sending the draft. It feels close to our style, so I don't want to start again. Could you make the offer pop a little more? The fifty percent discount is the reason we're posting this. Please keep the logo where it is, and show me two options for the offer rather than changing the whole design.",'What does “make it pop” mean here?',['Redesign the logo.','Emphasise the discount.','Replace the entire style.'],1,['What must stay in its position?','How many offer options does the client want?'],[['The logo.','Every text line.','The date only.'],['Two.','One.','Ten.']],[0,0],[['start again','Begin the design from the beginning.'],['rather than','Choose one action instead of another.']],'Clarify or confirm the requested emphasis and propose the two options.','I’ll keep the logo and overall style, then show two ways to emphasise the fifty percent offer. Would you prefer a size change in one version and a stronger color contrast in the other?')
clip('voice-scope','client','A second language version','Isha (Premium)',"Hello, the English poster is approved. We also need a version in Arabic for the campaign. I've got the approved translation, and my colleague can check the proof. I know we've used the two revision rounds already. Please send me the extra fee and the new delivery date before you begin. The brand mark should stay exactly as it is.",'What new work does the client need?',['An Arabic version.','A new brand mark.','Another English spelling check only.'],0,['Who can review the proof?','What must happen before work begins?'],[['The client’s colleague.','No one.','An unnamed generator.'],['Confirm the extra fee and delivery date.','Publish the current English draft.','Change the brand mark.']],[0,0],[['approved translation','The client has confirmed the exact translated wording.'],['before you begin','Agree on the additional work and terms first.']],'Confirm the new deliverable, the reviewer, what stays unchanged, and the quote.','I’ll quote for the Arabic version and confirm the new delivery date before starting. I’ll use the approved translation, keep the mark intact, and send a proof for your colleague’s review.')
clip('voice-update','client','A deadline with a missing detail','Lee (Premium)',"Hi, just checking on the first draft. Our team meeting is tomorrow afternoon, and I'd like something we can discuss there. It doesn't have to be the final version yet. Please tell me what is ready, what you still need from us, and when you'll send the preview. We're working in different time zones, so please include the time zone in your message.",'What does the client need before the meeting?',['A discussion preview and clear status.','A perfect final version immediately.','No update until after the meeting.'],0,['Does the preview need to be final?','What must the delivery time include?'],[['No. A discussion draft is enough.','Yes. All files must be final.','The client does not mention the issue.'],['The time zone.','Only “tomorrow”.','A random guess.']],[0,0],[['something we can discuss','A draft good enough for a team conversation.'],['what you still need','Name the information preventing progress.']],'Give an honest progress update. If you do not know the meeting time, ask rather than invent a deadline.','The layout is ready for discussion, but I still need the approved prices. What time is your meeting, and which time zone are you using? I’ll confirm when I can send the preview once we agree that timing.')
clip('voice-audience','client','A tone for the audience','Matilda (Premium)',"I've compared the two mood boards. The bright version is fun, but our daytime customers mostly come to read and have quiet conversations. I prefer the softer version for this poster. We can use a more energetic style for evening events later. For now, keep the invitation calm and make the practical details easy to find.",'Which direction fits this poster?',['The softer, calmer version.','The most energetic version.','A style chosen without considering the audience.'],0,['Who is this version for?','When might an energetic version be useful?'],[['Daytime customers who read and talk quietly.','Evening performers only.','A completely different business.'],['For later evening events.','Never under any circumstances.','For every daytime post.']],[0,0],[['for now','This is the current decision, not a permanent rule.'],['practical details','The information viewers need to act.']],'Recommend the current mood and distinguish it from the later campaign.','I’ll use the softer version for the daytime invitation and keep the practical details clear. We can develop an energetic version for evening events later. Could you confirm the opening time and location?')
clip('voice-editable','client','The file we need to edit','Daniel (Enhanced)',"The image looks good, but our staff need to change the price each week. Right now, all the words seem to be part of the picture. Could you send an editable version with the price in its own text layer? We use Canva here. A normal image preview would still be useful, but it won't replace the working file.",'What is the main unmet requirement?',['Editable price text in the working file.','A more dramatic photograph.','A completely new offer.'],0,['Which editor does the team use?','What does the client say about the normal image preview?'],[['Canva.','An unspecified paid animation program.','A spreadsheet only.'],['It is useful but does not replace the working file.','It is the only file needed.','It must never be delivered.']],[0,0],[['in its own text layer','The price must be separately editable.'],['won’t replace','The preview is not a substitute for the source.']],'Confirm the compatible source file and the separate preview.','I’ll prepare a Canva source with the price in a separate editable text layer and include a normal image preview. Could someone on your team test the price edit before I finalise the delivery?')
clip('logo-nike','logo','Nike: simplicity and interpretation','Jamie (Premium)',"Look at the Nike mark without the word. It is one curved shape, with a broader section at one end and a narrower tip at the other. The mark has very little internal detail, so we can still see its outline when it becomes small. To me, the curve suggests movement. That is an interpretation, rather than a fact the shape proves. In an analysis, describe the visible shape first, then explain what it may suggest and how it works at a smaller size.",'What does this analysis connect?',['A simple shape, small-size use, and a possible reading.','The company’s full financial history.','A claim that every curve has one fixed meaning.'],0,['Which observation is visible?','How is “movement” presented?'],[['The mark is a curved shape with little internal detail.','The mark must make everyone buy shoes.','The mark physically moves on the page.'],['As an interpretation.','As a historical fact about the designer.','As a guaranteed response from all viewers.']],[0,0],[['internal detail','Small features inside the outline.'],['to me','The speaker qualifies a personal interpretation.']],'Analyse the mark in three sentences: visible fact, possible reading, practical test.','I notice a single curved shape with little internal detail. To me, it suggests movement. I would test its outline at a small size before making a similar design choice for a new client.','Nike')
clip('logo-microsoft','logo','Microsoft: shape, space, and repetition','Zoe (Premium)',"The Microsoft symbol uses four colored squares. They sit in a two-by-two arrangement, with clear gaps between them. The repeated square shape and the regular spacing make the group feel organised to me. Notice that repetition does not require one color: the shape repeats while the colors differ. We can describe those choices without claiming that each color has one universal meaning. When analysing a new mark, ask which features repeat, which features change, and what remains recognisable when the mark is small.",'What repeats in this symbol?',['The square shape and regular arrangement.','Exactly the same color in every square.','A rough texture in every square.'],0,['How many squares are there?','What differs between the squares?'],[['Four.','Three.','Eight.'],['The colors.','The basic square shape.','The fact that they all touch without any gaps.']],[0,0],[['a two-by-two arrangement','Two rows and two columns.'],['while the colors differ','One feature changes while another stays consistent.']],'Describe two elements and one principle, then give a small-size test.','The symbol uses four square shapes with different colors. Repetition and regular spacing connect them as a group. I would test whether the gaps remain clear at a small size.','Microsoft')
clip('logo-amazon','logo','Amazon: the arrow as a visual clue','Isha (Premium)',"Look beneath the Amazon wordmark. The orange curved arrow starts under the letter A and points toward the letter Z. Those are visible details we can point to. Its curved shape may also look like a smile to a viewer. That is a reading of the shape, not proof of how everyone will respond. In a client explanation, separate what you can see from the meaning you suggest. Then ask whether the detail still reads clearly when the wordmark is small or shown in one color.",'What distinction does the speaker make?',['Visible details versus suggested meanings.','Free software versus expensive computers.','Real photographs versus handwritten notes.'],0,['Which letters does the speaker identify?','Which description is an interpretation?'],[['A and Z.','B and C.','M and N.'],['The arrow may resemble a smile.','The arrow is orange in this supplied version.','The arrow is under the wordmark.']],[0,0],[['points toward','Shows a direction to something.'],['may look like','Qualifies a resemblance rather than guaranteeing it.']],'Point to the arrow, describe its direction, and qualify one possible reading.','I can see an orange curved arrow beneath the wordmark, pointing from A toward Z. It may resemble a smile. I would check whether that detail remains clear at a small size and in one color.','Amazon')
clip('logo-mcdonalds','logo','McDonald’s: recognisable form with few details','Lee (Premium)',"The supplied McDonald's mark uses two joined arches that make an M-like shape. The color is yellow, and there is very little extra detail inside the mark. We can discuss shape and color as elements, and simplicity as a principle. Familiarity may help us recognise this particular mark, so recognition alone does not prove that any similar yellow shape would work for a new business. A designer still needs to check distinctiveness, clarity, and whether the mark fits the client's actual audience.",'Which design principle is discussed?',['Simplicity.','Adding as many details as possible.','Replacing the audience with the designer’s taste.'],0,['What basic shape does the speaker describe?','Why is familiarity mentioned?'],[['Two joined arches forming an M-like mark.','Four separate squares.','A circle shaded as a ball.'],['Recognition can depend on knowing the brand already.','A familiar mark proves all new marks will work.','Viewers never recognise a familiar brand.']],[0,0],[['very little extra detail','Few internal features to distract from the main shape.'],['does not prove','Avoids an unsupported conclusion.']],'Describe the mark and explain why a new client’s logo needs its own audience test.','I notice two joined arches and a yellow color. The simple shape has few internal details, but familiarity also helps me recognise it. A new mark still needs its own clarity and audience test.','McDonald’s')
Path(__file__).with_name('listening-curriculum.json').write_text(json.dumps(C,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2));print(len(C),'listening exercises authored')

